# ── KGSM cluster — read by every member on this host ──────────────────────────
# The secret every member of a cluster carries. It is what proves membership: a member trusts any
# caller bearing a service token signed with it.
#
# Every install is a cluster. On first install kgsm-base fills this with a generated secret when it is
# blank, and this machine founds a cluster of its own, its auth anchor holding the accounts. A machine
# joining a cluster somebody else runs takes that cluster's secret instead — before kgsm-base is
# installed, or by following kgsm-meta/NODE-PROVISIONING.md §10·a after, which switches this machine's
# own anchor off first.
#
# One file rather than one copy per member, because a machine runs more than one member: a node that
# runs the engine and game servers, and an anchor that provides one capability to the whole cluster.
# Each member's unit loads this BEFORE its own env file, so one could override it deliberately — but a
# member holding a different secret is one the others cannot authenticate, and nothing reports that as
# an error, because "not clustered" and "wrong secret" look identical here.

Cluster__Secret=

# Rotating: put the NEW secret above and the OLD one here, roll every member onto the new one, then
# clear this. Both are accepted while it is set, so a roll needs no downtime.
Cluster__SecretPrevious=
